<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb raw sugar imports down 46 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb raw sugar imports down 46 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's raw sugar imports in February totalled 62,072 tonnes, down 46 percent from a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.  </p>
<p>The breakdown was as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			   Feb 97     Jan 97	   Feb 96</p>
<p> Total		   62,072     112,212	  114,976</p>
<p>Main suppliers:</p>
<p> Thailand		45,803	35,274	   93,967</p>
<p> South Africa	     nil	23,447		nil</p>
<p> Australia	     16,269	53,491	   21,009</p>
<p>Total imports in the first two months of calendar 1997 reached 174,284 tonnes, against 202,419 tonnes during the same period of last year.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk (+81-3-3432-7391)</p>
</text>
